# UX 3.6 — contributor attribution (mandatory)

The UX 3.6 console layout is modelled on the community redesign by **@rathlinus**
(Linus Rath, UI/UX designer).

- Issue: <https://github.com/UNITRONIX/BetterDesk/issues/493>
- PR (design reference, **not** merged as a unit): <https://github.com/UNITRONIX/BetterDesk/pull/495>
- Last pre-Svelte reference commit: `d710bdbbb8541f325f6ecf8a24f7027187d475ba`

## Rules

1. **Never claim the redesign was merged.** UX 3.6 is an independent
   implementation in the existing EJS/JavaScript/CSS stack, built from that
   design as a reference.
2. **Every commit that ports, adapts, or refines UX 3.6 elements** must carry
   this line in the commit **body**:

   ```text
   Based-on: @rathlinus UX redesign (Refs #493, #495)
   ```

   Do not add it to unrelated commits. If the change also addresses a reporter
   issue, keep `Reported-by:` and the standard `Thanks:` supporter trailer.
3. **Keep credit visible in the repository**, not only in git history:
   - [`docs/development/CONTRIBUTOR-ATTRIBUTIONS.md`](docs/development/CONTRIBUTOR-ATTRIBUTIONS.md)
     — `@rathlinus` section describing exactly what informed UX 3.6.
   - [`docs/wiki/UX-3.5.md`](docs/wiki/UX-3.5.md) — operator-facing credit line.
   - Settings → General → Console interface shows `ux36.credits` in every locale.
4. **i18n:** the credit string `ux36.credits` must exist in all 26 locale files
   (see the web-nodejs i18n rule). Keep the `@rathlinus`, `#493` and `#495`
   tokens inside the translated sentence.
5. **Attribution scope:** design inspiration and navigation model. Do not
   attribute unrelated BetterDesk code to the contributor, and do not imply
   copyright assignment — see the licence section of the attributions file.

## Checklist for UX 3.6 commits

- [ ] Commit body contains `Based-on: @rathlinus UX redesign (Refs #493, #495)`
- [ ] Commit body still ends with the current `Thanks:` supporter line
- [ ] `CONTRIBUTOR-ATTRIBUTIONS.md` section updated if the scope of reuse grew
- [ ] Wiki credit and `ux36.credits` string still present in all locales
- [ ] No wording that suggests PR #495 was merged or that Svelte was adopted
